In this case, the absolute values reduce to \(x - 1\) and \(y - 1\), respectively. Therefore, the inequality becomes:
\begin{align*}
(x - 1) + (y - 1) \le 1
\end{align*}
Simplifying further, we get:
\begin{align*}
x + y \le 3
\end{align*}

